    "content": "\"DC\" most commonly refers to Washington, D.C. (District of Columbia), the U.S. capital and federal district, or DC Comics, the publisher of Batman and Superman. Other usages include direct current electricity, District Council, or \"da capo\" in music. Synonyms include the District, the Capital, or simply Washington.Key Usages and Examples:Geography (Washington, D.C.): The capital city, not a state, located between Maryland and Virginia. Examples include visiting the National Mall, the White House, or government proceedings.Media & Entertainment (DC Comics/Studios): A major American comic book publisher and studio producing films like Superman (2025) and Joker.Technology (Direct Current): A type of electrical current used in batteries and electronics (commonly paired with AC).Mathematics/Other: Refers to the Roman numeral 600 or \"da capo\" (from the beginning) in musical notation.Synonyms & Related Terms:For the city: The District, Washington, The Capital, D.C..For the publisher: DC Comics, DC Universe (DCU), Detective Comics.",
